 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the region heads, each measured by both; so is every Euclidean head, \
through the support of its vertex density"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"fd8ba02d-2e7f-44cf-ac04-a67437d8dcd2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d81c702-f00d-495e-81b1-a29c7f1a10f2"],
 ", Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b65070da-4ab4-4fba-ad1c-b19cf4f78b7e"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d84dd5d5-db79-43d0-bd80-672fe2c7c0e5"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular and hexagonal lattices, before the \
rim, and is the convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"40ef3259-2108-448c-8802-661ad8877dae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shell on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8ca101b-c635-46f7-b56f-9cc180340b42"],
 ", the coordination sequence; Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af8812f9-b2de-40a5-a65e-af3806155e83"],
 ", since a shell is all boundary."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"77cacd4d-7c69-4075-bc24-daae89adbc71"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Segment on the square grid between vertices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47c18302-cefe-4d43-b1e3-e508af368b7a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3deb8709-cbfa-49e8-a3a3-377993dd4d92"],
 " steps apart along the two axes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9e28c956-20b7-40bd-bde1-9d2f68598f81"],
 ": its interval is a rectangle, with counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5625c16c-f7a8-40ba-816b-73295c45356f"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ")"}], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e9c65c3-55fb-42cf-b9a2-ac80d92c688c"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a55f5111-ddb6-4745-b736-c2825f4adf93"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the discretized plane: the Riemannian measure can exceed the \
counting measure of the smaller ball, when a vertex at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f2394da-49ed-42f5-87eb-c4e9284b8ace"],
 " has no neighbour at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92722f83-aa77-4a67-b627-e0c4a443ac4a"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0542c14e-2680-45d3-8133-6ba7606dbd82"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["VolumeGrowthObservables"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/VolumeGrowthObservables", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "a2a09963-7287-4605-b488-211e2e57af8d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the dimension and the scalar curvature read from the growth of the balls \
under either measure; it lives on the Riemannian Infrageometry guide"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"81a3bec6-29da-4f05-bdf7-5729c4fc4a5d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Find Functions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"0c836b0e-e3a6-4e38-8d2b-346b13b41b3f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraPoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraPoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "c504abf2-b18b-4ce2-888b-3777ba3566c2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a vertex drawn from the candidate pool, narrowed by \"From\" and \"Distance\
\"; a trailing count gives a List of vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a2f04683-dc94-4016-b832-c313567517d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraMidpoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraMidpoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "6708dbfe-128c-449b-b7c6-6df088d8927e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the middle vertices of the shortest paths from p1 to p2 as a density, one \
vertex at even distance, two at odd"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"4a8976e9-59a3-47c9-88e3-0366d7717083"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraEquidistantSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraEquidistantSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "88f3f56b-286a-4906-93ec-3903dc1c75b1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the vertices equidistant from p1, \[Ellipsis], pn, as a sorted vertex list; \
a trailing {lo, hi} thickens each bisector to a slab"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9aae4921-9485-430b-a652-ce685c76a3ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraSphere"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSphere", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "0cfc2076-b3b4-491c-b7c4-4cf38ca9bdca"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "n inclusion-minimal connected subsets of the shell of c that separate its \
inside from its outside; Properties chooses the class, \"NextVertexFunction\" \
the order of the peel"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"3d868ade-c320-479d-b473-e0f75dbef74d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraSegment"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSegment", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "75391402-b7ae-4e43-ac08-315f96a5f732"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one shortest path from p to q as a vertex list; a trailing count gives a \
List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"62924761-4c17-4eaa-ac54-82f93e51b653"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRay"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRay", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "efa373fe-b6d2-45bc-8c21-154c6309135f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one ray from p through q as a vertex list, a shortest path from p through q \
that no neighbour of its last vertex prolongs; a trailing count gives a List \
of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"8a216b50-1d5f-45f8-b66c-72a1cc974ae6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraLine"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraLine", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "4848ad7a-64df-427b-a181-cb0fcb7a4d13"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one line through p and q as a vertex list, an inextensible shortest path \
through both; a trailing count gives a List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"bee6205d-fe33-4c9f-9170-3c6d2d2cb55e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Measurements", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"74c69309-4ec3-4ab3-9efd-b4005434726d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "8bc5e843-5175-48fc-a0b4-78ee8918aedd"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a property of a head on a graph: \"Graph\", \"Cardinality\", \"Length\", \
\"VertexDensity\", \"EdgeDensity\", \"Subgraph\", \"Faithful\", \
\"CountingMeasure\" and \"RiemannianMeasure\"; a List of properties gives an \
Association, All gives every property"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"58503b5a-e45c-4e72-8b09-9793f218e371"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDensity"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDensity", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "b1a0d57f-4c24-4eab-bc55-8448eb3a558e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the marginal of any shape to the vertex set with respect to the counting \
measure: a vertex, a vertex list, a density, a walk graph; the one coercion \
in the API"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"28c484e8-8f84-4555-967b-489ad358e54a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRepresentative"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRepresentative", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "721d9a63-de20-439f-9963-a5457557ab47"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one member of a head as a vertex list, read off its graph or found by its \
search; a trailing count gives a List of them, \"RandomChoice\" a random \
member"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f7b8b33c-5a6b-4657-9860-e2b3d989354c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMemberQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMemberQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "fe77a78a-cc68-4227-ab0e-8fa7142ba5cc"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "whether a vertex list is a member of a head on a graph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"5b5a4c89-dac9-46c7-9962-19420d9e251c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Substrates and Drawing", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"fdb4556c-29fd-4ecb-8eea-d5a2de4d2df8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrate"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrate", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "02e3da94-eab8-46f7-8fde-2da4abf4935a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the named example substrates at size \"Small\", \"Medium\" or \"Large\": \
the tilings, meshes and closed surfaces the other pages draw on; \
InfraSubstrate[] lists the roster"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"1f877558-4e65-4047-be04-564bc46f9a7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "9f04cf7d-382d-4374-8b9a-44c5a2df76b4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the summed densities of a list of objects drawn on a graph, the i-th object \
in the i-th palette color; a Directive styles the objects after it"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"16a6152c-3ea0-43ca-a872-be4711383c57"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Multi-constructions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"cdc8a0b0-9302-4b9f-ad61-ef1c49e36047"],

Cell["\<\
Whereas the causal graph of Euclidean constructions is causally invariant, \
the branchial graphs in infrageometry are non-trivial due to \
multi-constructions.\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"281ffa44-216f-4729-bd48-86732a07beae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "32a1718c-058f-4cd5-9558-42260d5bf417"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a construction stated before any graph: the objects, and hypotheses that \
construct them with inert heads or assert relations between them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"8a270320-f2ce-4d1a-8273-594ef7a51096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraStep"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraStep", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "350b203f-baef-4222-8e50-1eeb3f21e5c8"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one construction encapsulated as a step of a scene; a second argument \
labels it"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0a026331-0821-4c92-9ed2-92987f5bb54d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "398d8fb8-5624-4616-aeb3-51b5b118c225"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a scene solved on a graph, step by step; a List of bindings, one per \
admissible combination"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"598aefae-6c48-4fd2-b27e-03eda1cc4c23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSceneInstance"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSceneInstance", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "f924afa2-10e3-489d-a479-eaf67f82a06b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one solved binding of a scene; with an object name, reads that object out \
of it"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"fe183b6d-b065-4b6d-bc99-ae211bbf12be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSceneViewer"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSceneViewer", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "2f8695ea-7bb7-4bd1-b425-1db5b563c3ab"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a step-by-step view of a scene on a graph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9b49416c-caf9-46e5-9549-482891eff180"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Underlying graphs", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"914ae445-6b4e-4102-ac96-300391faf6fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SprayGraph"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/SprayGraph", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "fb326071-49d4-4e0e-8f11-929510ac6d5a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the breadth-first DAG rooted at c, whose source-to-sink paths are exactly \
the maximal shortest paths from c"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"6d5d81ce-1724-4449-a862-307566ed790f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Not here", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"7d3c2354-319e-4993-87b9-63771982266e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindBallHull"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindBallHull", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "7499373b-ed93-4b64-a5ec-7ae298638813"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the intersection of all balls containing a set of points; it lives on the \
Infra Topology guide"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"faa53e38-080c-4f14-b56e-77606cb158ba"],

Cell["\<\
not here: the quadric as an inert head and the layers of the convex hull; \
FindInfraQuadric stays on the Experimental guide\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"91c6517c-adef-41aa-a7c8-17320ccc5bdb"],

Cell["\<\
not here: an invariant of four points, the inverse of every head (the values \
of its unknowns for a given vertex set), and the graph of a line or of an arc \
as an exported name; none is in an item yet\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"71e170b8-f316-4d94-a4d6-52752340d52b"],

Cell["\<\
not here: the interactive multi-construction stepper in the causal and \
branchial direction; it stays on the Experimental guide\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"861edb8c-bc4b-4270-9a23-140a98f96f48"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

